{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":83561,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"13f58ab3-1850-4dff-a797-2755f43975ec","total_cost_usd":0.8204659999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61578,"cache_read_input_tokens":20278,"output_tokens":5968,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61578,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5968,"cache_read_input_tokens":20278,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61578},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":45237,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.045337,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5968,"cacheReadInputTokens":20278,"cacheCreationInputTokens":61578,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.775129,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"playtester\",\n  \"verdict\": \"targets_missed\",\n  \"summary\": \"The config as written cannot be flown — the ship fails to reach any band on ascent, the full hold lands hard at 5.45 m/s rather than the claimed 4.6, and the sweep confirms GDD 4.5 risk 1: multi-pass aerobraking is never cheapest, because the staged ballistic coefficient of 183 kg/m2 is too low for the atmosphere to brake rather than stop the ship.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ascent_fails_every_band\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.6\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params asserts a flight budget that closes: exhaust velocity 26000/11.7 = 2222 m/s, full tank 2222*ln(1750/850) = 1605 m/s against roughly 1450 m/s to the suborbital band, leaving about 61 kg of fuel and calling fuel_tank tier 1 the first purchase the profile asks for.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The simulator flew all three ascents and reached none of them. suborbital (65,000 m), low (115,000 m) and high (215,000 m) all report reached=false, why='crashed on ascent', fuel_remaining_kg 0, fuel_margin_pct 0. The exploration grid shows this is not a narrow miss of the design: bands_reachable holds in 64.2% of the 5,184 worlds and fuel_margin_sane in only 17.9%, so reachable-with-margin is the scarce combination, and the crew's world is outside it.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ablation_optimum_is_one_pass\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"GDD 2.3.1 requires the cheapest descent to be 2-4 committed passes, never a single plunge and never feathering. game_params concedes this for passes and substitutes skims, asserting optimal_skims of 0/1/2 by band from its own cost curve.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Across all nine band x load descents the cheapest pass count is 1, without exception: suborbital empty 15.2% of plate at 1 pass rising to 21.9 / 31.7 / 49.3 at 2/3/4; high band full hold 37.4% at 1 pass rising to 59.1 / 71.9 / 90.6. Cost is monotonically increasing in pass count everywhere. The cause is visible in the same rows — braking altitude climbs with pass count (suborbital empty 29,357 m at 1 pass to 37,776 m at 4) inside a 43,000 m atmosphere, so extra passes brake in thinner air and peak heat barely moves (70 to 74), leaving the thermal-cycling toll nothing to trade against. The grid agrees this is structural rather than mistuned: skimming_cools_the_entry holds in 43.8% of worlds but only at low ballistic coefficients (the top configs sit at 111.1, 33.3 and 11.1 kg/m2), and the crew's staged beta is 182.8.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"full_hold_lands_hard\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"landing.descent_speed_full_hold_ms is 4.6, derived in the balance notes as sqrt(2*1599*9.0/(1.5*1.8*504)) = 4.60 m/s, 0.4 m/s under the 5 m/s soft line, so a base hold lands soft and only greed past it does not.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Measured terminal velocity under the stated 504 m2 canopy at Cd 1.8 is 5.45 m/s, a miss of 0.85 m/s, and soft_landing=false in every full-hold descent in all three bands. The arithmetic differs because the sweep's full-hold mass is 2,247.8 kg, not the notes' 1,599 kg: measured cargo is 232.96 kg per slot against the notes' 124.9, giving a 1,397.8 kg hold and a full_hold_mass_ratio of 2.64 rather than the GDD 2.3.5 doubling. Half hold lands at 4.53 m/s and empty at 3.35, so the hard-landing line falls between half and full hold rather than beyond it. The grid says this is tunable: full_hold_lands_soft holds in 17.6% of worlds and in every one of the twelve top configs, all at 4.6 or 4.2 m/s.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"skim_cooling_far_weaker_than_priced\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier is [1.0, 0.851, 0.670, 0.411], described in the balance notes as the simulator's measured high-band array, still falling steeply at the third skim, and the whole cost_curve that places optimal_skims at 0/1/2 is built on it.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The sweep's measured high-band array at entry depth 0 is [1.0, 0.985, 0.971, 0.958] — three skims remove 4.2% of peak heat, not 58.9%. Low band measures [1.0, 0.975, 0.953, 0.932] and suborbital [1.0, 0.948, 0.891, 0.733]. Cooling also weakens with entry depth rather than strengthening: high band at 21,500 m entry depth measures [1.0, 0.989, 0.979, 0.971]. Against the params' own toll of 3.0*1.8^k, the first skim on the high band now buys 2.4 heat points (161.5 to 159.1) for 6.15 plate-percent, so optimal_skims collapses to 0 in every band and the entire cost_curve is unsupported. Skims also cost 0.53 to 0.51 hours each and 44-45 m/s of commit dv, which the ascent budget above does not have.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"difficulty_falls_with_band_not_rises\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"claim\": \"GDD 2.3.7 and the balance notes both require the return leg to get strictly harder with altitude — a suborbital descent burning 18.6% of plate flown optimally against 40.0% for a high-band one — and the params encode heat_index 78/100/130 by band.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Optimal-pass ablation falls with altitude at every load. Empty: suborbital 15.2%, low 13.9%, high 13.0%. Half hold: 28.9 / 26.1 / 24.1. Full hold: 44.3 / 39.9 / 37.4. Peak heat runs the same direction (full hold 117 / 111 / 108). The Researcher predicted the mechanism — entry speeds at a common periapsis are 1,316 / 1,366 / 1,441 m/s, a v^3 spread of only 1.31 — and here even that spread is swamped, because a higher band enters on a shallower path and brakes deeper (full-hold braking altitude 26,120 m suborbital against 23,098 m high) where drag is stronger per unit of speed shed. Cargo carries the curve instead: full hold costs roughly 2.9x empty in every band. The grid rates difficulty_rises_with_band satisfiable in 58.0% of worlds, so this is reachable, but not by band-indexed heat multipliers alone.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unstaged_pass_barely_exists_in_the_space\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"GDD 2.3.1 makes pre-stage coarse braking the intended first half of a descent — shallow passes with the naked hull while thrust remains to reshape the orbit between them — and reentry.unstaged_heat_multiplier of 3 prices it.\",\n      \"measured\": \"In the crew's own world it works: unstaged shallow passes peak at 69 (suborbital) and 76 (low) against a 100 capacity, both survivable. That is the one place the crew's config beats the grid — unstaged_pass_survivable is the rarest target in the space at 10.2% of 5,184 worlds, and not one of the twelve top-scoring configs achieves it (all report unstaged_peak_heat of 358-370, more than three times capacity, and all score 7 of 8 with this as the single miss). The crew's unstaged beta of 609.3 kg/m2 is what buys it, and any change that lowers ship mass or raises frontal area to fix the ablation or landing findings will spend it.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ballistic_coefficient_below_the_aerobraking_floor\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"4.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"The design assumes multi-pass aerobraking is a real manoeuvre, and the Researcher's ladder puts the staged full-hold ship at beta = 344 kg/m2, inside the 300-500 real-capsule band.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The sweep measures staged beta at 182.8 kg/m2 and unstaged at 609.3 — the staged figure is 47% below the Researcher's derivation, because measured cargo mass and the assumed ship mass disagree (232.96 kg per slot against 124.9). This is the quantity that controls the pass-count finding: the top grid configs that do satisfy skimming_cools_the_entry sit at 111.1, 33.3 and 11.1 kg/m2, and at 33.3 and below the measured multiplier arrays flatten ([1.0, 0.828, 0.828, 0.828]) because the first contact removes the orbit outright — the charter's floor of roughly 50 kg/m2, visible in the data.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\n      \"current\": 900,\n      \"proposed\": 1400,\n      \"reason\": \"Every ascent crashed with zero fuel remaining, and raising the tank is the smallest move that buys delta-v without touching thrust or the mass budget the landing findings depend on; it costs launch cost realism and makes fuel_tank tier 1 a smaller upgrade than the shop currently assumes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.thrust_n\",\n      \"current\": 26000,\n      \"proposed\": 34000,\n      \"reason\": \"At 1400 kg of fuel the liftoff TWR falls to 1.15, below the point where gravity losses eat the extra tank, so thrust rises with it to hold TWR near 1.5; it costs the thruster tier 1 upgrade its headroom, which should be repriced upward.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"landing.parachute_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": 504,\n      \"proposed\": 710,\n      \"reason\": \"Measured full-hold terminal velocity is 5.45 m/s against a 5.0 m/s soft line at the sweep's real 2,247.8 kg full-hold mass; 710 m2 gives sqrt(2*2247.8*9.0/(1.5*1.8*710)) = 4.59 m/s, restoring the base-hold-lands-soft promise, and it costs the Storage/Parachute pairing its bite until the parachute tiers are repriced above it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier\",\n      \"current\": [1, 0.851, 0.67, 0.411],\n      \"proposed\": [1, 0.985, 0.971, 0.958],\n      \"reason\": \"The stated array is described as measured but the sweep's high-band measurement is [1.0, 0.985, 0.971, 0.958]; replacing it makes the params honest, and it costs the entire cost_curve its basis, which is the point of the next two changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.cycle_toll_growth\",\n      \"current\": 1.8,\n      \"proposed\": 1.0,\n      \"reason\": \"With real cooling of 1.5% per skim there is nothing for a steeply growing anti-feathering toll to trade against, and GDD 4.5 risk 1 names exactly this fallback — flat per-pass ablation with a hard cap on passes; it costs the U-shaped optimum, which the simulator says does not exist at this flight model.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.optimal_skims\",\n      \"current\": {\"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 1, \"high\": 2},\n      \"proposed\": {\"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 0, \"high\": 0},\n      \"reason\": \"Recomputing the params' own cost formula against the measured multipliers puts the minimum at zero skims in every band, so the field should state what the flight model does rather than what the design wants; it costs the skim framing its role as the replacement for the retired 2-4-pass rule.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.heat_index\",\n      \"current\": {\"suborbital\": 78, \"low\": 100, \"high\": 130},\n      \"proposed\": {\"suborbital\": 100, \"low\": 108, \"high\": 118},\n      \"reason\": \"Measured optimal-pass ablation falls with altitude (44.3 / 39.9 / 37.4 full hold), so a rising index is fighting the simulator rather than describing it; these values re-establish the GDD 2.3.7 rising curve on top of measured behaviour, and cost the suborbital band its cheap descent, which is where a new player learns.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.bands.2.altitude_min_m\",\n      \"current\": 150000,\n      \"proposed\": 400000,\n      \"reason\": \"The Researcher's own note says the band-to-band heat spread is only 1.31x and that moving the high band far out is the lever; raising its floor is the only change that makes altitude itself carry difficulty, and it costs orbital period — the high band's period passes an hour, making the time warp a hard requirement rather than a convenience.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"cargo.base_slots\",\n      \"current\": 6,\n      \"proposed\": 6,\n      \"reason\": \"Left unchanged deliberately: measured cargo is 232.96 kg per slot giving a 2.64x full-hold mass ratio against GDD 2.3.5's doubling, and the per-slot mass belongs to the Debris Designer's catalog rather than to this object — flagged here so the discrepancy is not fixed twice.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_notes\": [\n    \"The ascent failures are the least diagnosable result in the sweep. 'crashed on ascent' with zero fuel remaining is consistent with an underfuelled ship, but also with a gravity-turn profile the simulator flies badly; the flight budget in the balance notes closes on paper by roughly 155 m/s, which is a thin enough margin that a slightly lossy ascent model would erase it. Treat the direction of the tank and thrust proposals as sound and the exact magnitudes as a first bracket to be re-swept, not a candidate to commit.\",\n    \"The skim multiplier disagreement is the single most consequential finding and I cannot rule out that the params' array came from a different measurement than the one in this sweep — the balance notes cite [1.0, 0.851, 0.670, 0.411] explicitly as measured high-band values, and this sweep measures [1.0, 0.985, 0.971, 0.958] for the same band at the same nominal entry depth. Either an earlier sweep measured a different quantity (the charter warns that skim depth and entry depth were conflated once before) or the flight model changed underneath the params. Both are worth resolving before the cost_curve is rebuilt.\",\n    \"Ballistic coefficient is reported two ways that disagree by a factor of two: the sweep measures staged 182.8 kg/m2 while the Researcher derives 344 and the balance notes derive 344 from a 1,599 kg full hold. The sweep's own cargo figure of 232.96 kg per slot is the reconciling number and it does not match the Debris Designer's 124.9. Every mass-dependent finding here — the parachute, the pass costs, the full-hold ratio — inherits that disagreement, and it should be settled before the parachute area is enlarged, because a smaller true hold mass would make 710 m2 an overcorrection.\",\n    \"Nothing in this report is evidence about anxiety, and the reentry pillar in GDD 3.3 is the thing most at risk from the proposals above. A larger parachute, a flatter ablation toll and zero optimal skims together make the descent more forgiving and less of a decision; the simulator cannot see that cost. The plasma-to-chute window in particular is measured here only as a touchdown speed, never as a duration a player waits through.\",\n    \"The simulator is a point mass with a perfect pilot: no attitude error, so the off_retrograde_penalty of 1 is never exercised; no debris collisions, consistent with the GDD cut but meaning hull risk is landing-only in the model as well as the design; and no notion of the EVA layer at all, so every tether, shear and jetpack claim in the params is unmeasured by this sweep and should not be read as verified by it.\",\n    \"The exploration grid's satisfaction rates are computed over a uniform sweep of the seven axes, not over a plausible design space, so a low rate means 'rare in this box' rather than 'impossible'. unstaged_pass_survivable at 10.2% is the clearest case: the crew's config achieves it comfortably at peak heats of 69 and 76 while no top config does, which says the grid's box is centred somewhere the crew's world is not, and that the two should not be compared target-by-target without that caveat.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":81280,"ttft_stream_ms":2420,"time_to_request_ms":223,"type":"result","duration_ms":81297,"uuid":"47c42a0f-4810-4a3a-af6b-a7053ffc70ca"}
